    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0515" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Four Power Pact/114</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-06-06">June 6,
                        1933</date>.<lb/>[Received June 21.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegrams No. 54 of
                    June 2nd, 11 a.m., and No. 56 of June 3rd, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d304-f1"/> on the situation of the Four Power Pact, I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith a memorandum of the conversation I had with the
                    Undersecretary of State for Foreign Affairs, Signor Suvich, on which telegram
                    No. 56 of June 3rd, 7 p.m., was based.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Breckinridge Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d304-a1.xml" xpointer="d304-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
